    "note": "2026-10-19 refresh: day tags for all 108 billing slots, from the By Day tab of the official lineup page (orlando.edc.com/lineup), read three ways that agree slot for slot: the page's HTML, a Firecrawl render of it, and the by-day poster image on the same page (edco_2026_mk_lu_lubd, uploaded 2026-07-07, read visually). 36 slots a day, no act on two days, nothing cancelled or removed since July. Changes from the 2026-07-07 file: (1) two new Friday slots, \"Josh Baker\" and \"Prospa\", billed solo on the poster beside \"Prospa B2B Josh Baker\" (all three are separate lines on the poster and the page, so all three are entries here); (2) two acts the official billing now spells differently keep their frozen pick keys, because a rename would orphan every pick on them: \"Marlon Hoffstadt\" is billed \"Marlon Hoffstadt (Sunset Set)\" (Sunday), and \"Luke Dean B2B Max Dean\" is billed \"Max Dean B2B Luke Dean\" (Saturday). Billing extras already inside older names (\"(Sunset Set)\", \"(Wholesome Riddim Set)\") stay as they were frozen. Dates unchanged: November 6-8, 2026 at Tinker Field (site header, 2026-10-19). No stages or set times yet: orlando.edc.com/set-times is a 404 and the lineup page has no times. When to expect them: for 2025 (Nov 7-9) Insomniac posted the three daily set-time graphics in late October (EDM Identity re-hosted them from its 2025/10 uploads; its guide ran 2025-11-05) and listed hours of 1 PM to midnight daily, so the 2026 times should land on orlando.edc.com and the Insomniac app around the last week of October. When they do, follow docs/fest-update-runbook.md: freeze first, keep these spellings, stages from the official map. History: the 2026-07-07 research read the A-Z tab only (106 slots); it noted that the June 23 press release differed slightly (brand placeholders, and a then-missing ChaseWest, Holy Priest, M81!, Maddix, Monoky, Ravenscoon) and trusted the live page. \"Discovery Project\" is Insomniac's emerging-artist showcase slot, not one act."
